      "side": 1,
      "message": "Issue: When bmcActiveFirmwareId is unknown (e.g., getActiveBmcFirmware failed — it swallows errors with console.log) or when the active BMC entry is not marked Updateable, the getter silently defaults to the first inventory member. That may be a BIOS image, a CPLD, or a backup BMC slot depending on the ordering returned by bmcweb.\n\nImpact: The commit message explicitly promises \"The dropdown defaults to the bmc_active entry to preserve existing behavior.\" In the fallback path, it does not — the user may unknowingly upload firmware to whichever inventory member Redfish happened to list first.\nRecommendation: Return null in the fallback so the dropdown forces an explicit selection (or keeps the store action\u0027s legacy Targets \u003d [bmcPath] behaviour). This also removes the \"surprise target\" risk without breaking systems that expose bmc_active.",
      "range": {
