      "side": 1,
      "message": "The dropdown is the right product change, but the Redfish-first source for allowable Targets is now UpdateServiceCapabilities (AllowableTargets / AllowableStaging), not a reconstructed list from FirmwareInventory.\n\nSee [DSP0268 2026.1](https://www.dmtf.org/sites/default/files/standards/documents/DSP0268_2026.1.html#updateservicecapabilities-100)\n[Schema](redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/UpdateServi…Capabilities.v1_0_0.json)\nAdded in DSP8010 2025.2 (UpdateService v1.16.0).\nFollow `UpdateService.UpdateServiceCapabilities` when present; fall back to FirmwareInventory members with Updateable\u003dtrue (and empty Targets) on bmcweb, which does not implement this resource yet.  We need to discuss adding this to bmcweb as this has been coming up a lot lately.  \n\nAlso: already mentioned but defaulting to FirmwareInventory/bmc_active (or the first Updateable member) is not equivalent to today’s Manager URI (getBmcPath()). Those are different bmcweb code paths.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "35277ff10da6fe1d5d0fcebe0139bcdcaea4d00b",
