      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T03:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This item is not a blocker since the [Redfish-first design](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/94472) has not been ratified, but here is the gist:\n\nRedfish-first\nThis new Vuex shape remaps SoftwareInventory into a parallel camelCase row\nThat is the pattern redfish-first.mdc asks us not to grow, suggestions:\n\n* Keep @odata.id, Id, Name, Description, Version, Updateable, Status, RelatedItem\n* Collection name is FirmwareInventory, not updateableInventoryItems\n* Prefer `Id \u003d\u003d\u003d bmcActiveFirmwareId` over `location.endsWith(\u0027/\u0027 + id)`\n* `Name` is the Redfish display property. OpenBMC often sets `Name` to \"Software Inventory\" for every member, so Description (Id) is a reasonable label, but keep the resource intact and derive the label in the view\n* Include `Version` (and running vs backup if you already know it). Two BMC images with the same Description are otherwise indistinguishable\n* Discover UpdateService from ServiceRoot (useRedfishRoot), then UpdateService.FirmwareInventory[\u0027@odata.id\u0027], instead of hardcoding /redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory in new code\n\n`RelatedItem[0].@odata.id.split(\u0027/\u0027).pop()` for BMC vs BIOS is pre-existing and already drops SPI/CPLD from the cards. The dropdown is how those members become visible — another reason to keep full SoftwareInventory objects instead of a third mapped list.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "35277ff10da6fe1d5d0fcebe0139bcdcaea4d00b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
